// Hand-authored Phase 2 dev cron config for the single-tenant OpenClaw
// container, bind-mounted read-only as ~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json (see
// infra/docker-compose.dev.yml).
//
// CORRECTED per docs.openclaw.ai/cli/cron and /automation/cron-jobs (see
// docs/openclaw-integration-notes.md): this repo originally assumed a job's
// `prompt` is injected "as if a channel message arrived." That's wrong — the
// documented model is an unattended scheduler-run agent turn, explicitly NOT
// a simulated channel message. The docs describe `openclaw cron add` as the
// supported interface, with the cron expression and message as *positional*
// args (not `--cron`/`--message` flags as originally guessed), a `--session
// main|isolated|current|session:<id>` target, and `--agent <id>` to pick the
// agent. They do not publish the on-disk jobs.json schema this file guesses
// at, so the field names below (`schedule.type/expression/timezone`,
// `agent`, `prompt`) remain UNVERIFIED against a real install. The
// CLI-equivalent command, using `--session isolated` for a fresh transcript
// per run and `--no-deliver` since delivery happens via the digest skill's
// own MCP tool call rather than a channel reply:
//
//   openclaw cron add "0 8 * * *" \
//     "Run the digest skill now for the daily period." \
//     --tz America/New_York --agent dev-org-primary \
//     --session isolated --no-deliver
//
// If bind-mounting this file doesn't work against a real openclaw build,
// switch Phase 1/2 dev to running that `openclaw cron add` command once
// inside the container instead (see docs/phase1-runbook.md).
{
  jobs: [
    {
      id: "dev-org-daily-digest",
      schedule: { type: "cron", expression: "0 8 * * *", timezone: "America/New_York" },
      agent: "dev-org-primary",
      // Starts an unattended scheduler-run agent turn (not a simulated
      // channel message) — the agent should recognize this as "run the
      // digest skill now" and follow its SKILL.md steps.
      prompt: "Run the digest skill now for the daily period.",
    },
  ],
}
